# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 4 of the Tutorial (Part 2)

[B11's Example 8.29]

r4,0,a,4
r2,0,b,2
r6,a,b,6
rb,a,c,3
ra,b,c,3

analysis: dc
note: Find the equivalent resistance of the resistor network between nodes 0 and c — the walkthrough circuit from Part 1, in the compact form the rest of the practice set uses.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/b11e0829.jpg [408px]
tool: er
n1: 0
n2: c
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes


